{
  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "e00000",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "RAG Playground - chunking notes",
      "order": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00001",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Why chunk boundaries matter",
      "order": 1,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A retriever never sees a document. It sees chunks, and it can only return what",
      "order": 2,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00003",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "a chunk contains. If the sentence that answers a question is split across two",
      "order": 3,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00004",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "chunks, neither half may score well enough to be retrieved, and the generator",
      "order": 4,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00005",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "is left to guess. Boundary placement is therefore a recall decision disguised",
      "order": 5,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00006",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "as a preprocessing step.",
      "order": 6,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00007",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Token counts in this note come from the heuristic counter, not a model",
      "order": 7,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00008",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "tokenizer.",
      "order": 8,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00009",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fixed windows",
      "order": 9,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00010",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The simplest strategy cuts the text every N tokens with an overlap of M",
      "order": 10,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00011",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "tokens. It is predictable and cheap, and every chunk has the same cost to",
      "order": 11,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00012",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "embed. It is also blind to structure: a window will happily start in the",
      "order": 12,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00013",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "middle of a table row or end halfway through a definition.",
      "order": 13,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00014",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Page 1 of 3",
      "order": 14,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00015",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "RAG Playground - chunking notes",
      "order": 15,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00016",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Recursive character splitting",
      "order": 16,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00017",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Recursive splitting tries a list of separators in order: blank lines, then",
      "order": 17,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00018",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "single newlines, then sentence ends, then spaces. It only falls back to a",
      "order": 18,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00019",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "finer separator when a piece is still larger than the budget. The result",
      "order": 19,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00020",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "respects paragraphs where it can and sentences where it must, which is why it",
      "order": 20,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00021",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "is the default in most frameworks.",
      "order": 21,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00022",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Heading-aware sections",
      "order": 22,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00023",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A heading-aware chunker starts a new chunk at every heading and carries the",
      "order": 23,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00024",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "heading path into the chunk metadata. This only works when the parser reports",
      "order": 24,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00025",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "headings. A plain text extractor returns every line as a paragraph, so the",
      "order": 25,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00026",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "chunker sees one long section and falls back to its token budget.",
      "order": 26,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00027",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Page 2 of 3",
      "order": 27,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00028",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "RAG Playground - chunking notes",
      "order": 28,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00029",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Overlap and its cost",
      "order": 29,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00030",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Overlap protects answers that straddle a boundary, but every overlapped token",
      "order": 30,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00031",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "is embedded and stored twice. At an overlap of twenty percent the index grows",
      "order": 31,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00032",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "by a quarter, and near-duplicate chunks start to crowd each other out of the",
      "order": 32,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00033",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "top results unless a reranker such as MMR spreads them.",
      "order": 33,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00034",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Token counts in this note come from the heuristic counter, not a model",
      "order": 34,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00035",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "tokenizer.",
      "order": 35,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00036",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "What to measure",
      "order": 36,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00037",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Compare strategies on the same parsed document. Count chunks, look at the",
      "order": 37,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00038",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "token distribution, and check recall at ten on a fixed question set. A",
      "order": 38,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00039",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "strategy that wins on one corpus can lose on another, so the comparison is the",
      "order": 39,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00040",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "result, not the ranking.",
      "order": 40,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00041",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Page 3 of 3",
      "order": 41,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": null,
